>
> I see the guaranteed fixed-range you originally proposed as
> potentially having this problem.  Walk/jump along until you're
> surrounded, teleport past the annoying stuff, repeat.  No?

The problem already exists; people walk along, jump past monsters, and
keep going.  The concept of 'very fast' is still sufficiently fast that
almost no monsters can keep up.  That is a different problem from the
one I'm looking at right now, however.  The stairwell proposes the
biggest problem, even though it's near-guaranteed to be flooded with
monsters most of the time.

